# Deploy-profile operator quickref

Thin Shell Phase **4bj** — operator-facing path for **image / single-tenant** builds. Phase **4bw** expands **staging ops** (Gap Closure D.4 / D.5) without changing monorepo defaults.

The monorepo **default** install stays full-trunk (Wave I.7/I.8 honesty).

## When to use

| Context | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Local / CI monorepo | Do **nothing** — full trunk |
| Single-tenant image / staging web | Opt in with deploy-profile APPLY |

## Commands (inspect / apply)

```bash
# Inspect (hermetic full-trunk without APPLY)
pnpm run print:deploy-profile-plan
pnpm run print:deploy-profile-env

# Image / staging — triple opt-in (see remediation Gap Closure D)
WORKSPACE_DEPLOY_PROFILE_APPLY=1 \
WORKSPACE_DEPLOY_PROFILE=denali \
  pnpm run apply:deploy-profile -- --write
# … next build …
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry   # restore full-trunk artifacts — do not commit filtered outputs
```

## Staging ops (Phase 4bw)

Staging web builds already honor deploy-profile when **APPLY=1**. Operators should treat these scripts as the SOT for VPS staging — do not hand-edit IgnorePlugin env in production unit files.

### Env gates

| Env | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `WORKSPACE_DEPLOY_PROFILE_APPLY=1` | Enables profiled ALLOW env + optional `--write` apply |
| `WORKSPACE_DEPLOY_PROFILE` | Comma-separated workspace ids / package names (`full` / `*` = no filter) |
| *(unset APPLY)* | Legacy staging: `ALLOW_DENALI_WEB_PLUGIN=true` only (D.4) |

### Scripts

| Script | Behavior with APPLY=1 |
| --- | --- |
| `scripts/vps-deploy/resolve-staging-web-plugin-allow-env.mjs` | Prints `export ALLOW_*=…` from live plan (D.4) |
| `scripts/vps-deploy/sync-staging-web-build.sh` | Local `next build` → rsync `.next`; runs `apply:deploy-profile --write` then restores registry (D.5) |
| `scripts/vps-deploy/sync-staging-web-vps-build.sh` | Rsync source → VPS `next build`; same apply/restore on remote (D.5) |
| `scripts/vps-deploy/build-operator-vps.sh` | Operator VPS image path — apply/restore when APPLY=1 |

### Staging recipe (single product)

```bash
export WORKSPACE_DEPLOY_PROFILE_APPLY=1
export WORKSPACE_DEPLOY_PROFILE=denali   # or urban,starter,…
# Local build + rsync .next:
bash scripts/vps-deploy/sync-staging-web-build.sh
# Or build on VPS after rsync source:
bash scripts/vps-deploy/sync-staging-web-vps-build.sh
```

After APPLY builds: scripts restore via `pnpm run generate:workspace-registry`. **Never commit** filtered transpile / guest-runtime / register artifacts.

### Verify without VPS

```bash
pnpm run print:deploy-profile-plan
pnpm run print:deploy-profile-env
node --test scripts/test/resolve-staging-web-plugin-allow-env.spec.mjs
node --test scripts/test/staging-deploy-profile-ops.spec.mjs
```

## Do not

- Delete product packages from default `apps/web` `devDependencies` to “look thinner”
- Commit filtered transpile / guest-runtime / register artifacts from APPLY runs
- Treat opaque plugin loaders as defects — they are the §2.4 registry
- Skip registry restore after APPLY `--write` (leaves trunk dirty)

